#!/bin/sh
# Versioned pre-commit hook (ini-3nzc). Activated per-clone by
# `git config core.hooksPath scripts/hooks` — which `make install-hooks` does,
# and which the scaffold does automatically for checkouts it creates.
#
# One source of truth: the old install copied this content into each clone's
# hooks dir, and 6 of 8 fleet checkouts simply never ran the copy step. A
# versioned hook can change fleet-wide in one commit; activation is one local
# config bit that the tooling sets.
#
# ENV SCRUB, learned from this hook's own first invocation, which correctly
# BLOCKED the commit that introduced it: git exports GIT_DIR / GIT_INDEX_FILE
# etc. while running hooks, and everything the check suite spawns inherits
# them — nested git in tests operates on the WRONG repo ("core.bare and
# core.worktree do not make sense"), and go build's VCS stamping fails the
# same way. Scrubbing here fixes the class for every current and future test
# that shells out to git, instead of requiring each test to remember.
unset GIT_DIR GIT_WORK_TREE GIT_INDEX_FILE GIT_PREFIX GIT_COMMON_DIR GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY
#
# WHY check-fast AND NOT check (ini-7ts2, operator decision 2026-09-12): this
# hook used to run the full `make check`, ~2.5 minutes, on every commit. What
# commit time catches that nothing else would within minutes is a commit that
# does not COMPILE reaching main (ac12e59) -- and that is seconds of build and
# vet. The tests it also ran were duplicated twice over: by `make check` after
# the rebase (the only run that sees the tree actually being pushed; the hook
# fires BEFORE the rebase, so a collision is invisible to it by construction)
# and by CI at the pushed sha. What tests here could never catch: rebase
# collisions, env-gated rigs, races (-race is CI-only). One engineer paid five
# post-rebase cycles landing one fix while main moved; the hook's copy of the
# suite was the part that bought nothing. The lints and censuses stay: they
# are the guards for silent-omission classes (a test tagged off a platform, a
# rig nobody runs, a target nothing invokes) and cost about a second.
#
# THE SUITE STILL RUNS BEFORE EVERY PUSH: `make check` after `git pull
# --rebase`, immediately before `git push` -- root CLAUDE.md, unchanged. Do not
# put `test` back here "for safety" without answering the paragraph above.
make check-fast
